NAME: a pointer read and written through @, < and >
DESCRIPTION: MOV through @p, <p and >p: each writes the B-field of the cell p names, < and > moving p; see behtests/indirection_modes.beh
SRC:
(let (p 3)
  (seq
    (MOV 7 (Ind p))
    (MOV 8 (Dec p))
    (MOV 9 (Inc p))
    (JMP 0)
    (DAT 0 (store p))
    (DAT 0 0)
    (DAT 0 0)
    (DAT 0 0)))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

  MOV.AB #7     , @_LET1 
  MOV.AB #8     , <_LET1 
  MOV.AB #9     , >_LET1 
  JMP    #0     , #0     
_LET1 
  DAT    #0     , #3     
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     